# GUIShop Item Lifecycle

This document covers how items flow through the system: loading, editing, and saving.

## Loading Flow

### On Plugin Enable (Preload)
```
GUIShop.onEnable()
  → ConfigManager.initConfigs() - loads YAML files
  → PlayerListener preloads all shops:
      for each shop in shops.yml:
        new Shop(shopName).loadItems(true)  // preLoad=true, no GUI created
```

### When Player Opens Shop
```
PlayerListener.openMenu()
  → GUIShop.getCREATOR().remove(player)  // Clear creator mode!
  → new Menu(player).open()
      → Menu.loadItems(false)
          if loadedMenu == null: loadMenuFromConfig()
          else: use cached loadedMenu
      → Menu.loadMenu() - creates PagedGui with ItemStacks
      
Player clicks shop button:
  → new Shop(player, shopName, menuInstance).open()
      → Shop.loadItems(false)
          if shop not in loadedShops: loadShopFromConfig()
          else: use cached shopItem
      → Shop.loadShop() - creates PagedGui with ItemStacks
```

## Creator Mode Flow

### Entering Creator Mode
```
/gs edit [shopname]
  → GuishopCommand adds player to GUIShop.getCREATOR()
  → Opens Menu or specific Shop in creator mode
```

### Creator Mode Click Handling (Shop.java / Menu.java)
```
Left-click: Allow normal item movement (drag/drop)
Right-click OR Shift+Left-click: Open ItemEditorGui for that item
```

### Item Editor Save Flow (CRITICAL)
```
ItemEditorGui.saveAndClose():
  1. Auto-convert types:
     - DUMMY with prices → SHOP
     - SHOP without prices/commands → DUMMY
  
  2. Apply all values to ItemStack via PDC
  
  3. saveToConfig(item):
     a. Item.parse(item) - reads PDC into Item object
     b. Item.serialize() - converts to Map for YAML
     c. Save each property to FileConfiguration
     d. Write to disk: shopConfig.save(file)
     e. UPDATE IN-MEMORY CACHE DIRECTLY:
        shopItem.getPages().get(pageKey).getItems().put(slot, parsedItem)
     
  4. onSave callback runs:
     a. Add player back to CREATOR set
     b. this.loadItems(false):
        - Sets this.GUI = null (forces rebuild)
        - Gets shopItem from cache (already updated!)
        - Calls loadShop() to create new GUI
     c. this.open(player) - shows fresh GUI
```

### Exiting Creator Mode
```
Shop/Menu.onClose():
  if in creator mode:
    if !clickOverride:  // Not opening editor
      saveCreatorInventory()  // Saves drag-dropped items
    ALWAYS: GUIShop.getCREATOR().remove(player)
```

## Key Insight: Cache-First Updates

When saving from ItemEditorGui, we:
1. Save to config file (for persistence)
2. Update in-memory cache directly (for immediate display)
3. Rebuild GUI from updated cache

This avoids needing to reload from disk and ensures instant updates.

## Item Type Rules

| Type | Has Prices | Has Commands | Has Target Shop | Behavior |
|------|------------|--------------|-----------------|----------|
| DUMMY | No | No | No | Decoration only, no interaction |
| SHOP | Yes | No | No | Can be bought/sold |
| COMMAND | Maybe | Yes | No | Runs commands on purchase |
| SHOP_SHORTCUT | No | No | Yes | Opens another shop |

**Auto-conversion in ItemEditorGui.saveAndClose():**
- If DUMMY but has prices → becomes SHOP
- If SHOP but no prices/commands/target → becomes DUMMY
